UPDATE companies SET description='D Volt Co. was founded in 2022 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas. The company operates as a U.S.-based power solutions provider offering fully integrated services from engineering design and precision manufacturing to direct sales and customer support.

The company manufactures, sells, rents, and repairs transformers and electrical equipment. Its product lines include three-phase and single-phase pad-mount transformers, overhead transformers, dry-type transformers, power transformers, auto reclosers, switchgear, breakers, switches, and accessories. With a vertically integrated model, D Volt Co. controls engineering, manufacturing, and assembly in the United States for distribution-size transformers, and reports more than 1,000 units in operation with a typical lead time of eight weeks.

D Volt Co. serves utilities, data centers, renewable energy projects, and industrial clients across North America. The company also provides testing, maintenance, and field repair services to support installed equipment.

The company emphasizes its vertically integrated structure as a differentiator, enabling control over speed, quality, cost efficiency, and customization. All products are built to UL, DOE, and CSA standards, and the firm highlights short lead times, design flexibility, competitive pricing through global sourcing, and in-house engineering support.', certifications=ARRAY['UL','DOE','CSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Transformer manufacturing", "Switchgear manufacturing", "Electrical equipment repair", "Field service and maintenance", "Engineering design", "Precision manufacturing", "Custom design modification", "Compliance testing (UL, DOE, CSA)", "U.S. assembly of distribution-size transformers", "Transformer rental", "Direct sales and customer support"], "industries": ["Utilities", "Data centers", "Renewable energy", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8 weeks", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated model controlling speed, quality, cost, and customization", "UL, DOE, and CSA certified products", "U.S. assembly for distribution-size transformers", "Eight-week typical lead time", "Custom design modifications and in-house engineering"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2022, headquartered in Houston, Texas -> /about", "Manufactures, sells, rents, repairs transformers and electrical equipment -> /", "Product lines: three-phase pad mount, single-phase overhead, single-phase pad mount, dry-type, power transformers, auto recloser, switchgear, breakers, switches, accessories -> /", "1,000+ units running, 8 weeks lead time -> /", "Vertically integrated model with engineering design, precision manufacturing, direct sales, customer support -> /about", "Capable of assembling in the U.S. for distribution-size transformers -> /about", "Serves utilities, data centers, renewable energy projects, industrial clients -> /about", "Offers testing, maintenance, repair services -> /about", "Products comply with UL, DOE, CSA standards -> /about", "Short lead times, customization, competitive pricing, in-house engineering, global sourcing -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufactures, sells, rents, repairs transformers and electrical equipment", "founded_year": "2022", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='d-volt-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='D&V Electronics is an engineering company based in Auburn Hills, Michigan, that designs and manufactures advanced testing systems for electrical powertrain components. The company focuses on performance, endurance, and production testing for the automotive, aerospace, marine, and railway sectors.

Its product line includes complete test systems for starters, alternators, inverters, power electronics, e-motors, and e-axles, serving both internal combustion and electric or hybrid vehicle platforms. Beyond hardware, D&V provides universal software applications that can be rapidly configured for custom test sequences, along with on-site calibration, maintenance, and training services. The company notes that its testing systems operate around the clock at installations worldwide.

D&V serves original equipment manufacturers, tier-one suppliers, retail and aftermarket operations, military organizations, universities, and the remanufacturing industry. Its systems are used in warehouse and retail environments for component verification as well as in high-volume production and endurance validation.

