UPDATE companies SET description='Dakota Outerwear Co. operates from Minot, North Dakota, located two miles north of the city on Highway 83 and five miles south of Minot Air Force Base. The company traces its roots to 1988, when it began producing American-made military outerwear. It is 100% veteran-owned and managed; the team is led by Jesh, a 12-year Army veteran who deployed in support of Operations Iraqi Freedom and Enduring Freedom, and includes Gary, a 30-year oilfield veteran, along with Tammy and Brendon handling inside sales and logistics.

The company fabricates its own branded line of military outerwear — jackets, parkas, bibs, and coveralls — using domestic labor and North Dakota resources. It also represents a full line of flame-resistant workwear for the oilfield, electricians, mine workers, and welders, meeting standards such as NFPA 70E, NFPA 2112, and ASTM F1506. Beyond manufacturing, Dakota Outerwear provides embroidery services for custom uniforms and runs a retail storefront.

Primary customers include the U.S. military, National Guard, law enforcement agencies, and federal, state, and local government organizations. The company also serves oilfield companies, electrical contractors, mining operations, and welding shops that require FR protective gear. Individual buyers, including first responders and recreational users, can purchase hats, boots, gloves, coveralls, uniforms, underwear, and individual equipment directly.

