UPDATE companies SET description='Diamond Electric Mfg. Corp. traces its roots to 1937, when Inosuke Tomita founded Diamond Electric in Japan. The company established its U.S. presence in 1990 with Diamond Electric United States (DEUS) in Dundee, Michigan, led by first president Nobu Hashimoto. In 1996, ground broke on a new plant in Eleanor, West Virginia, where mass production of ignition coils began in 1997. The Eleanor facility held its grand opening in 1998 and has since expanded multiple times. Today the corporate office remains in Eleanor, while a sales and design center operates in Farmington Hills, Michigan, near Detroit’s automotive hub.

The company designs, manufactures, and distributes automotive electrical components, specializing in ignition coils. Its capabilities span design engineering, research and development, manufacturing, and thorough product testing. Multiple U.S. locations provide manufacturing, sales, and support for global OEM customers. The Eleanor plant handles high-volume coil production, while the Farmington Hills center focuses on design and customer collaboration.

Diamond Electric serves three primary customer groups: OEM automotive manufacturers, service-part retailers, and DIY installers. It has earned quality awards from major automakers, including a President’s Product Quality Award from Subaru of Indiana Automotive in 2004. The company also supports community initiatives in Putnam County, West Virginia, where it was named Corporate Citizen of the Year in 2005.

The business is guided by a philosophy that prioritizes trust, superb quality, and the happiness of all stakeholders. Core values include customer focus, community involvement, integrity, teamwork, open communication, and safety. Diamond Electric emphasizes partnering with stakeholders as the key to the future, delivering products on time and defect-free through dedicated teamwork and constant improvement.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design engineering", "Research and development", "Ignition coil manufacturing", "Product testing", "Distribution", "Sales and technical support"], "industries": ["Automotive OEM", "Automotive aftermarket", "Service part retail", "DIY/installer", "Automotive electrical", "Automotive ignition products"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1937 by Inosuke Tomita -> /about", "US operations began 1990 with DEUS in Dundee, MI -> /about", "Eleanor, WV plant groundbreaking 1996, production 1997, grand opening 1998 -> /about", "Corporate office in Eleanor, WV; sales/design center in Farmington Hills, MI -> /", "Designs, manufactures, distributes automotive electrical components (ignition coils) -> /", "Serves OEM automotive manufacturers, service part retailers, DIY installers -> /", "Quality awards from major automakers (Subaru of Indiana Automotive 2004) -> /about", "Putnam County Corporate Citizen of the Year 2005 -> /about", "Certifications: ISO 14001, IATF 16949 -> db", "Philosophy: trust, quality, customer focus, community involvement, integrity, teamwork, safety -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Diamond Electric designs, manufactures, and distributes automotive electrical components.", "founded_year": "1937", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='diamond-electric-mfg-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Diamond Medical Equipment & Supply operates from a showroom at 300 South Rodney Parham in Little Rock, Arkansas. The company states it has more than 40 years of experience in the home medical equipment market, though a specific founding year is not published. Ownership structure and founder names are not disclosed in the available information.

The business functions as a retail supplier and distributor of home medical equipment and supplies, carrying products from manufacturers such as Pride Mobility and Golden Technology. Its showroom offers power chairs, lift chairs, scooters, and other mobility aids for purchase or rental. The company also provides repairs, parts, and white-glove delivery that includes setup and tutorial within Central Arkansas. It describes itself as one of the area''s largest retail suppliers and claims the largest showroom in the state.

Customers include individuals, caretakers, medical professionals, nursing homes, and assisted living facilities. Diamond Medical bills Medicaid, all PASSE programs, and major medical insurance plans directly. The staff assists with verification of medical necessity and payment options.

