UPDATE companies SET description='Diaz Sheet Metal, LLC was established in 2005 in Hyattsville, Maryland. The company operates as a licensed and insured mechanical contractor specializing in sheet metal fabrication, HVAC systems, and plumbing services for commercial and residential clients across the state.

The shop produces custom spiral duct, flat oval duct, and precision fittings using CNC plasma cutting and automated coil lines, working with galvanized steel, black iron, 304/316 stainless steel, and aluminum. Full 3D CAD modeling and shop drawing services feed directly into fabrication, ensuring compliance with SMACNA standards and a tolerance of ±0.01 inch. Beyond fabrication, the firm installs and maintains rooftop units, VAV systems, split systems, heat pumps, boilers, and ductless mini-splits, and provides plumbing services including drain cleaning, repiping, sewer repair, and hydro jetting.

Customers include Maryland contractors, facility managers, and homeowners. Project examples range from commercial HVAC system installations and industrial ventilation upgrades to custom spiral ductwork for commercial layouts, main sewer repairs, and cooling tower servicing. The company partners with Trane and Carrier for equipment supply.

The company emphasizes a rapid response guarantee with a sub-two-hour reaction time for critical failures, a zero-defect policy, and BIM coordination to resolve field conflicts before installation. Its stated goal is to provide the gold standard of technical service to the local community with absolute precision and rapid response.', certifications=ARRAY['ENERGY STAR','ASTM A653','ASTM A653/G90','OSHA','EPA 608 Universal']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom spiral duct fabrication", "Custom flat oval duct fabrication", "Precision fitting fabrication", "CNC plasma cutting", "Automated coil line processing", "3D CAD modeling and shop drawing", "BIM coordination", "SMACNA standards compliance", "HVAC system installation (rooftop units, VAV, exhaust, split systems)", "HVAC maintenance and emergency repair", "Heat pump and boiler installation", "Ductless mini-split installation", "Plumbing services (drain cleaning, pipe replacement, sewer repair, hydro jetting, repiping, water heater installation)", "Cooling tower service", "Custom metal fabrication (galvanized, black iron, 304/316 stainless steel, aluminum)"], "industries": ["Commercial HVAC", "Industrial Ventilation", "Residential HVAC", "Plumbing", "Energy-efficient cooling solutions"], "materials": ["Galvanized steel", "Black iron", "304 stainless steel", "316 stainless steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["CNC plasma cutting systems", "Automated coil lines"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Emergency response <2 hours; same-day priority for urgent orders", "tolerances": "\u00b10.01 in", "built_on": ["Rapid Response Guarantee: sub-two-hour reaction for critical mechanical failures", "Custom duct fabrication to SMACNA standards with \u00b10.01 inch tolerance", "Full 3D CAD modeling and shop drawing services with direct CNC export", "Authorized partner for Trane and Carrier HVAC equipment", "20+ years of trade experience with OSHA and EPA 608 certified technicians"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 -> /about", "Headquarters Hyattsville, Maryland -> db", "Custom fabrication of spiral duct, flat oval duct, and precision fittings -> /", "CNC plasma cutting and automated coil lines -> /", "Materials: galvanized, black iron, 304/316 stainless steel, aluminum -> /", "Tolerance \u00b10.01 inch -> /", "SMACNA standards compliance -> /", "3D CAD modeling and shop drawing services -> /", "HVAC installation and maintenance (rooftop, VAV, split systems, etc.) -> /", "Plumbing services (drain cleaning, repiping, sewer, hydro jetting) -> /", "Partners: Trane/Carrier -> /", "Rapid Response Guarantee: <2 hour reaction -> /", "OSHA Certified, EPA 608 Universal technicians -> /", "ENERGY STAR certification -> db", "ASTM A653/G90 standard -> /", "MD License #88432 -> /", "20+ years trade experience -> /", "Zero defect policy, BIM coordination -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Custom fabrication of spiral duct, flat oval duct, and precision fittings.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='diaz-sheet-metal-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Digitron Semiconductors operates from Kenilworth, New Jersey, where it manufactures high-reliability discrete semiconductor devices. The company focuses on Zener diodes, transient voltage suppressors, rectifiers, and transistors tailored to stringent military, aerospace, industrial, and commercial requirements.

The product portfolio spans thousands of part numbers across categories such as TVS devices (2 W to 100,000 W), bridge rectifiers (2 A to 35 A), Zener diodes (250 mW to 100 W), and various transistor types including BJTs, JFETs, MOSFETs, SCRs, and triacs. Digitron emphasizes a high-mix, low-to-mid-volume production model with reasonable lead times and an internal test laboratory capable of MIL-PRF-19500 JANTX-equivalent screening, environmental stress testing (temperature cycling, burn-in), and customized test flows. All quality levels receive lot-based test reports and certificates of compliance.

Customers include defense and aerospace contractors, industrial equipment manufacturers, and commercial electronics producers. The military/aerospace grade meets full robustness for harsh environments, the industrial grade offers extended temperature operation and higher endurance, while the commercial grade undergoes four levels of 100% inspection achieving a 0.99998 assurance level for less stressful applications.

Digitron positions itself as a risk-mitigating supplier by combining broad product availability, stable year-over-year pricing, and a quality system registered to AS9100:2016 and ISO 9001:2015. Its quality policy targets on-time delivery and continuous improvement on every order, supported by source-control drawing accommodation and in-house delta and PDA calculations.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100:2016','ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High reliability processing flow (MIL-PRF-19500 JANTX equivalent)", "Environmental stress screening (temperature cycling, burn-in)", "Customized test flow development", "Delta and PDA calculations", "Lot-based test reporting", "Certificate of Compliance issuance", "Source control drawing accommodation", "Full temperature range testing", "100% inspection (four levels) for commercial lots", "In-house test laboratory operations"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense/Military", "Industrial", "Commercial electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to mid volume runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["MIL-PRF-19500 JANTX equivalent high-reliability screening", "Customized test flows and source control drawing support", "In-house environmental test laboratory (temperature cycling, burn-in)", "High-mix, low-to-mid volume production with stable pricing", "Four-level 100% inspection for commercial lots (0.99998 assurance)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Kenilworth, NJ -> db", "Product portfolio: Zener diodes, TVS, rectifiers, transistors -> /", "Quality levels: military, aerospace, industrial, commercial -> /quality", "Certifications: AS9100:2016, ISO 9001:2015, RoHS -> /quality, db", "High reliability processing flow with MIL-PRF-19500 JANTX equivalent -> /quality", "Environmental testing (temperature cycling, burn-in) -> /quality", "Customized test flows and source control drawings -> /quality", "In-house test laboratory -> /quality", "Lot-based test reports and Certificate o