UPDATE companies SET description='Direct Wire, based in Denver, Pennsylvania, was founded in 1977 as a small business operating from a home garage in Pennsylvania. The company has grown into a profitable U.S.-based manufacturer of wire and cable systems and assemblies, maintaining a commitment to domestic production and ethical, sustainable operations.

The company manufactures a broad portfolio of wire and cable products under flagship brands such as Flex-A-Prene®, Ultra-Flex®, All-Flex®, Veri-Flex®, and Dura-Flex®, serving welding, power, industrial, data center, renewable energy, battery, and entertainment applications. Direct Wire also produces oxygen-free copper rod and stems in 8 mm and 12.5 mm diameters at its Lancaster facility. In-house capabilities include cable assembly, proprietary compound coloring, longitudinal stripe extrusion (pioneered in 2000), inkjet and indent printing, a repair and spark-testing program, copper recycling, private labeling, and same‑ or next‑day fulfillment from distribution warehouses in Denver and Lancaster.

Direct Wire serves industries including renewable energy (solar, wind, EV charging, battery storage), industrial and OEM, power and renewables, data centers, welding, battery and motive power, entertainment and stage lighting, vehicle and transit, oil, gas, and mining, distribution, rental equipment, and appliance and electronics. Customers cited include Michigan CAT, IWS Gas and Supply, and ILMO Products Company.

The company emphasizes its U.S.-based manufacturing heritage as a differentiator, citing shorter lead times, job creation, and higher quality. Its “Service. Technology. People.” philosophy is backed by an on-site quality laboratory that conducts testing to UL, ASTM, SAE, and MSHA standards, and by proprietary rubber and plastic compounds engineered for durability.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed','RoHS','ASTM standards','SAE standards','MSHA approved']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable manufacturing", "Cable assembly", "Oxygen-free copper rod production (8 mm, 12.5 mm)", "Cable coloring with proprietary compound colorants", "Longitudinal stripe extrusion", "Inkjet printing on cable jackets", "Print wheel (contact) printing", "Indent printing (debossed marking)", "Cable repair and spark testing", "Copper recycling", "Private labeling", "Order fulfillment and distribution", "Custom cable design and engineering"], "industries": ["Renewable Energy", "Industrial & OEM", "Power & Renewables", "Data Centers", "Welding", "Battery & Motor", "Entertainment", "Vehicle & Transit", "Oil, Gas, & Mining", "Distribution", "Rental Equipment", "Appliance & Electronics", "Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Oxygen-free copper rod and stems", "Proprietary rubber compounds", "Proprietary plastic compounds", "Copper wire and cable (for recycling)"], "equipment": ["High-speed inkjet (non-contact) printing systems", "Print wheel (contact) printing systems", "Indent printing equipment", "Copper rod manufacturing line (8 mm and 12.5 mm)", "On-site quality laboratory test equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same or next business day for stock orders", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same- or next-business-day shipping on stock orders", "Pioneered permanent longitudinal stripe extrusion in 2000", "On-site quality laboratory with UL, ASTM, SAE, and MSHA testing capabilities", "Copper recycling program with COMEX-based credits applied to future orders", "U.S.-based manufactu