UPDATE companies SET description='Dyna Tool & Mold, Inc. operates from Kearney, Nebraska. The company traces its roots to 1989 when Randy Damratowski and Darren Yendra each invested $5,000 and borrowed $25,000 to open a shop in Grand Island with a manual mill, saw, lathe, and surface grinder. In 1995 the business relocated to Kearney and built a 7,250‑square‑foot facility, which was expanded by 4,500 square feet in 2006. After Damratowski’s passing, the company was acquired in October 2019 by Iowa Mold & Engineering of Belle Plaine, Iowa, under president Brad Cook.

The shop specializes in designing and building plastic injection molds, including single‑cavity, multi‑cavity, multi‑core‑pull, hot‑runner, automatic unscrewing, and large molds suited for presses up to 1,500 tons. Beyond moldmaking, it offers custom precision machining, wire EDM, gun drilling, tool and die work, prototyping, and full mold repair and maintenance.

Dyna Tool & Mold serves manufacturers throughout the Midwest. The source material does not specify particular industries or name individual customers.

